    <h3 style="text-align: center; background-color: #ff2e63;"">RULES AND REGULATIONS</h3>
    <h5>Membership</h5>
    <p>Any Marian Engineering College student can apply for the membership of Mechatronics Club. A nominal fee decided by the core comitee will be collected as registration fee at the time of joining.</p>
<h5>Benefits of Joining Club</h5>
<p>Mechatronics Club have a workspace were you can use a large number of microcontroller boards like arduino, raspberry pi, nodemcu ,other electronics devices, sensors,drives etc , mechanical tools like welding  machine ,grinding ,drilling and other mechanical tools also we have computer facility. </p>
<p>Students of club gets a price reduction for various events conducted by the club.</p>
<p>Students gets project development assist from the club coordinators and other members.</p>
    <h5>Core committee Members.</h5>
    <p>The Governing Council is elected to manage the affairs of the Club. It consists of <br> President -1 <br>  Vice – Presidents – 1 <br>  Secretary – 1 <br>  Treasurer – 1 <br>   Media Coordinator-1 <br>  Management Coordinator-2 <br>  Program Coordinator-2 <br>   Technical Coordinator-2 <br> Department Coordinator-5 <br> Staff Incharge-1 <br> Staff departmental coordinators-5 <br> the elected members have a time period of 1 year to show their potentials in club by organizing programs like workshops , competitions  ,industrial visits,Seminars, and other activities. </p>
    <h5>Duties and Responsibilities</h5>
    <p><b>President</b> <br> To preside over the meetings of the Club <br> To issue instructions and directions club To advice the Club about its activities.<br><b>Vice President </b> <br> To assist the President to execute his functions effectively <br>  To execute the functions of the President in his absence <br><b>Secretary</b>   <br> To keep and maintain the records, registers, accounts, and files of the Club<br>
To convene the meetings of the Youth Club in consultation with the President <br>
To look after the day to day functioning ofthe Club <br>
To receive and send letters and other communications on behalf of the Club. <br>
<b>Treasurer </b> <br>To operate joint accounts of Club and transaction of money with the concurrence of the executive committee.<br>
</p>



